WEBVTT

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:04.560
In this video I want to show how to activate tail detection.

00:00:05.100 --> 00:00:08.380
That is an extra feature of CowCatcher AI.

00:00:09.100 --> 00:00:10.860
We have the detectors.

00:00:11.640 --> 00:00:14.820
You now have the current one probably switched on in CowCatcher.

00:00:15.500 --> 00:00:17.140
So detecting calving.

00:00:18.380 --> 00:00:20.300
And then we press add a detection.

00:00:21.300 --> 00:00:24.180
And then we press here on CowCatcher Tail Up.

00:00:24.480 --> 00:00:26.900
So CowCatcher, tail up detection.

00:00:26.900 --> 00:00:32.500
Then you select your four cameras, or the cameras of your calving pen.

00:00:34.340 --> 00:00:38.260
Then you connect your Telegram again.

00:00:38.480 --> 00:00:39.120
Those are already set up.

00:00:39.840 --> 00:00:43.060
If it was saved properly from the previous one, so you only need to click the current one.

00:00:43.180 --> 00:00:46.220
I don't have them switched on right now, because it's a dummy account.

00:00:47.620 --> 00:00:50.280
Nowadays we can turn on an alarm via the app.

00:00:50.480 --> 00:00:51.480
That's something for another video.

00:00:52.200 --> 00:00:53.860
Actually, it's quite simple now.

00:00:53.860 --> 00:00:55.160
You click save.

00:00:56.300 --> 00:00:56.860
And then there are now...

00:00:56.900 --> 00:01:02.380
...two detectors here, so CowCatcher and the tail detection, Tail Up.

00:01:03.380 --> 00:01:04.580
Then we go to monitoring.

00:01:04.780 --> 00:01:08.680
Then you also see that all four cameras are monitoring neatly again.

00:01:09.180 --> 00:01:15.380
And under the cameras heading you now also see the second detector next to the camera.

00:01:16.080 --> 00:01:24.020
So on these four dummy cameras it runs both a calving detection and a tail-up detection.

00:01:25.060 --> 00:01:25.800
And that was it.
